/home/sat/mcrl-v025-floor-ws/gpt.md:100:[PROPOSAL] **Method and comparators.** Preserve LC-SRS, \(\lambda=118424222.8550065\) bit/J, \(\kappa=10097071012.757404\) bits, their frozen hexadecimal representations, C3View, 67–64–64–1 scorer, optimizer, S/R/C loss, and 2,000 updates. Fit INFORMED and MATCHED-PLACEBO only: 48 models. Retain ZERO-SURFACE \(B=Q1+Q2\) and TEACHER-ORACLE diagnostics. Preserve gate §7’s training-world strata, cyclic permutations, unchanged held-out labels, and ≥80% placebo eligibility per fold. No sign-reweighted training or candidate variants.
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-floor-ws/gpt.md:112:Predictions remain \(Q3(s_r,a_r)-Q3(s_r,a_r^{ref})\). Require both classes in every world and ≥24 unique rows per class overall; insufficient support stops observability without replacement sampling. Zero predictions are errors. Small/zero targets, unsupported, reference, control, and masked rows remain separately accounted for, outside sign denominators. Nonfinite labels/predictions invalidate execution; undefined correlations fail their existing predicate.
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-floor-ws/gpt.md:124:[INFERENCE] Principal risks are minority-class scarcity, placebo-preserved generic propensity, dependence on one Q12 lineage, teacher information outside deployable inputs, calibration mismatch, and simultaneous actions invalidating reference topology. Balanced accuracy addresses class weighting alone (`authority/LC-SRS-GATE-CONTRACT.md`, §§3, 7, 9–12).
