/home/sat/mcrl-v025-strategic-fable-ws/ADJUDICATION-fable-2026-09-10.md:139:**Against §4.1 (third wall).** "The off-policy corpus is a known defect on the owed-repair register; `EXACTGEN2` will regenerate; a corpus built around the fixed point fixes it." Response: regenerating around a head-independent fixed point is exactly the fix, and it is a **contract change** — A3 defines `a⁰` as the learned argmax, so a fixed-point reference redefines the route labels. That makes it option 4 by another name. And it does not change the bound: whatever the reference, the routes share `≤1.3%` above it.
