/home/sat/mcrl-v025-strategic-fable-ws/DECOMP-fable-2026-09-10.md:92:3. It **forfeits "a learned interaction head enables coordination"** as an ablatable route. Coordination becomes a comparator statement (FULL vs the per-user-argmax seed; FULL vs S_UNI; contract §C4 style), not a source ablation. Under the panel harness the coordination prize is unreachable for any decomposition (round-1 Theorem 2 still holds there); under S-cat its ceiling is the exact argmax over the sealed bounded catalogue.
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-strategic-fable-ws/DECOMP-fable-2026-09-10.md:100:- **Multi-start headroom survives the reporting numerator (9.87% SEALED, 3.56% MARGIN_Q below the best endpoint).** This is search-order and seed headroom over the deployed reference, reachable by exact search. It bounds what any learned score can add *through the panel harness*: the harness's ceiling is a first-improvement fixed point from its seed, and that headroom is exactly the gap between such fixed points and the best one found. It is not a route's prize.
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-strategic-fable-ws/DECOMP-fable-2026-09-10.md:136:Answer: yes. Under the panel harness the term decomposition's ceiling is exact unilateral search, i.e. what S_UNI already reaches, plus the multi-start seed/order headroom that no head controls. That is an acceleration claim ("reaches a stated fraction of the unilateral prize within budget"), not a coordination claim. I do not dispute N4; I state it as the ceiling.
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-strategic-astra-ws/controller-records/V025-CONTROLLER-ADJUDICATION-STRATEGIC-STOPLIST-2026-09-10.md:24:- The bounded-search advantage is **not** a mathematical ceiling. Its comparator is one specified unilateral procedure's local fixed point, not the best obtainable by every unilateral strategy and not a certified global optimum. The claim is that coordinated moves improve those certified local endpoints.
