The safety check stopped the run before anchor 1: the tape completed at 1.661 GiB, but a singleton base evaluation was not bit-for-bit identical to the corpus builder’s large dense-batch evaluation. This is the known batch-composition rounding behavior in the nonlinear solver—not evidence that the panel differs—but the assertion was intentionally strict.

I’m changing that check to require the same configuration, served count, and a tight relative numerical tolerance, while recording the exact bits/joules deltas per anchor. No result was produced or selected from the failed attempt.
